{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "simulation Phase 3 (#841): sm.setnoise(mode='tsys-manual') scenarios, run by CASA and by casa-rs",
  "notes": [
    "Each noisy scenario's noise is its DATA minus its noise-free twin's. A tsys-manual term has a σ per row, so compare_sm_ms.py divides each implementation's noise by CASA's formula (tsys_manual_sigma, with each antenna's elevation of the field at the row's TIME) and checks unit variance per correlation and class, a KS test between the two, and casa-rs's variance over CASA's in groups of rows (spectral window, dish pair, auto or cross, eight time bins), each within five standard errors.",
    "tsys-predict observes from 2 h before transit to 50 min after, at 52 to 67 degrees elevation: earlier, alma.cycle10.3's antennas shadow one another and the two simulators flag different ones (docs/CASA (C++) bugs.md); from 1 h after transit on 2026-03-21 the two simulators' UVW differ by 3.7 to 4.6 mm, against at most 0.001 mm before; the cause is not established and is not noise (the other scenarios' spans keep within 1 mm).",
    "The scenarios observe at 40 degrees elevation and above, where CASA's airmass, which it caches for 100 s of solution times, differs from the airmass at each integration by under 0.1 % of Tsys; casa-rs computes it at every integration (docs/CASA (C++) bugs.md). Each scenario has one integration time, so CASA's EXPOSURE of the first row is every row's.",
    "Model images are named relative to the oracle's --model-root, as in sm_predict_scenarios.json: alma-big/model4 is 512 pixels of 0.15 arcsec centred on (0.0007615435494667714, -0.0001523087098933758) rad with one plane per channel of the 4-channel 230 GHz band. tsys-predict checks that CASA's noise-scaling T scales the noise only, not the predicted model.",
    "tsys-mixed has dishes of 12 m and 7 m, autocorrelations, two spectral windows of 32 channels at different frequencies and channel widths (one decreasing) and tsys-manual's other parameters away from their defaults (rxtype 1 doubles Tsys).",
    "tsys-openfromms is simobserve's thermal-noise flow: observe, close, openfromms, setseed, setnoise(mode='tsys-manual'), corrupt. casa-rs reopens CASA's first stage (openfromms_ms casa), so the rows are CASA's."
  ],
